.TH "HTMLINPUTELEMENT.COLORSPACE" "3JS" "March 2, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLInputElement.colorSpace \- HTMLInputElement: colorSpace property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]colorSpace\f[B]\f[R] property of the
\f[CR]HTMLInputElement\f[R] interface reflects the \f[CR]<input>\f[R]
element\(cqs \f[CR]colorspace\f[R] attribute, which indicates whether
the color space of the serialized CSS color is \f[CR]sRGB\f[R] (the
default) or \f[CR]display\-p3\f[R].
It is only relevant to color controls.
.SH VALUE
A string containing the value of the \f[CR]colorspace\f[R] attribute.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Getting and setting color spaces
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]input\f[R] id=\(dqcolor\-picker\(dq type=\(dqcolor\(dq colorspace=\(dqdisplay\-p3\(dq alpha />
.EE
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] colorInput = document.getElementById(\(dqcolor\-picker\(dq);
console.log(colorInput.colorSpace); \f[I]// \(dqdisplay\-p3\(dq\f[R]
colorInput.colorSpace = \(dqlimited\-srgb\(dq; \f[I]// convert to srgb\f[R]
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]<input type=\(dqcolor\(dq>\f[R]
